{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_fdf290a452864ced86a1f493","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 206 lines\n460:   (when-some [session (get (:sessions @acceptor) attachment)]\n461:     {:reader (:ring session) :writer (:handle session)}))\n462: \n463: \n464: ;; =============================================================================\n465: ;; The dialing peer (section 5: the link over its dialed attachment)\n466: ;; =============================================================================\n467: \n468: (defn dial\n469:   \"Compose the dialing end of one WebSocket channel (3.1). `:attach!`\n470:    is the dao.stream.ws/make-attacher product whose :traffic deposit\n471:    medium is the same medium named by `:traffic` (its target), with\n472:    `:cursor` already minted on it before any attach!; `:ring` is the\n473:    channel ring buffer this end projects onto. `:table` names the\n474:    identities this peer serves over the dialed channel, so\n475:    `dial-step!` runs the projection and then this end's own mirror\n476:    step: the dialing end serves the other direction on the same\n477:    connection. `dial-attach!` takes a remote descriptor whose\n478:    :dao.stream/channel is this channel's ws descriptor: it attaches,\n479:    projects the attachment onto the ring, and answers through\n480:    dao.stream.remote/attacher with the channel end {:reader ring\n481:    :writer handle} -- the link's drain then runs inside every\n482:    reflection operation. One dial value carries one active\n483:    attachment; a reattachment composes a fresh dial with a fresh\n484:    cursor, as dao.stream.ws.md composes one medium per active client\n485:    attachment. `:names`, optional, is the name map beside `:table`\n486:    that this end's mirror answers named requests from. `dial-resolve!`\n487:    resolves a name through the dialed channel before any reflection\n488:    exists. :dao.stream.remote/events, :dao.stream.remote/resend-after,\n489:    :dao.stream.remote/budget, :dao.stream.remote/drain-budget,\n490:    :dao.stream.remote/max-outstanding, :dao.stream.remote/max-filed and\n491:    :dao.stream.remote/give-up-after pass to the attacher as its policy.\n492:    `:step-budget`, `:mirror-budget` and `:chase-budget`, optional\n493:    positive integers or nil, bound `dial-step!`'s projection and\n494:    mirror per tick, as for make-acceptor.\"\n495:   [{:keys [attach! traffic cursor ring table names step-budget\n496:            mirror-budget chase-budget] :as opts}]\n497:   (when-not (and (fn? attach!)\n498:                  (map? traffic)\n499:                  (stream/writer? (:dao.stream/handle traffic))\n500:                  (stream/reader? (:dao.stream/handle traffic))\n501:                  (some? cursor)\n502:                  (stream/reader? ring)\n503:                  (stream/writer? ring)\n504:                  (stream/closable? ring)\n505:                  (map? table)\n506:                  (or (nil? names) (map? names))\n507:                  (pos-int-or-nil? step-budget)\n508:                  (pos-int-or-nil? mirror-budget)\n509:                  (pos-int-or-nil? chase-budget))\n510:     (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream ws dial composition\"\n511:                     {:opts opts})))\n512:   (let [channel (atom nil)\n513:         mirror-cursor (atom (:dao.stream/cursor\n514:                               (stream/cursor ring stream/anchor-oldest)))\n515:         policy (select-keys opts [:dao.stream.remote/events\n516:                                   :dao.stream.remote/resend-after\n517:                                   :dao.stream.remote/budget\n518:                                   :dao.stream.remote/drain-budget\n519:                                   :dao.stream.remote/max-outstanding\n520:                                   :dao.stream.remote/max-filed\n521:                                   :dao.stream.remote/give-up-after])]\n522:     (atom {:attach! attach! :traffic traffic :cursor cursor :ring ring\n523:            :table table :names names :channel channel\n524:            :mirror-cursor mirror-cursor :policy policy\n525:            :step-budget step-budget :mirror-budget mirror-budget\n526:            :chase-budget chase-budget})))\n527: \n528: \n529: (defn- establish!\n530:   \"The ws attach of the channel descriptor `cd`, the attachment's\n531:    projection onto the ring, and the remote links over the channel end\n532:    {:reader ring :writer handle}, recorded as the dial's one channel.\n533:    Nil once established; a channel attach that fails answers the ws\n534:    attacher's own outcome and records nothing. A dial already stepped\n535:    at a `now` steps the new link at it first, so the requests the\n536:    attachment sends at once carry deadlines.\"\n537:   [dial cd]\n538:   (let [{:keys [attach! traffic cursor ring channel policy now]} @dial\n539:         r (attach! cd)]\n540:     (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n541:       r\n542:       (let [handle (:dao.stream/handle r)\n543:             ls (remote/links\n544:                  (merge policy\n545:                         {:dao.stream.remote/channels\n546:                          {cd {:reader ring :writer handle}}}))]\n547:         (when (some? now)\n548:           ((:step ls) cd now))\n549:         (reset! channel {:cd cd\n550:                          :attachment (:dao.stream/attachment r)\n551:                          :handle handle\n552:                          :project (projection\n553:                                     {:attachment (:dao.stream/attachment r)\n554:                                      :traffic (:dao.stream/handle traffic)\n555:                                      :cursor cursor\n556:                                      :ring ring})\n557:                          :reflect! (:attach ls)\n558:                          :resolve! (:resolve ls)\n559:                          :step! (:step ls)})\n560:         nil))))\n561: \n562: \n563: (defn dial-attach!\n564:   \"Attach one reflection of `descriptor` (a :dao.stream/remote\n565:    descriptor) through the dialed channel: the ws attach runs first,\n566:    the attachment's projection is composed, and the remote attacher\n567:    answers with the reflection -- its confirmation deferred, per\n568:    dao.stream.remote.md 2.4, to the descriptor probe the link sends\n569:    now. A channel attach that fails answers the ws attacher's own\n570:    outcome. One dial value carries one active attachment: a dial that\n571:    has already attached rejects a further dial-attach! -- its ring\n572:    and traffic cursor already belong to the first attachment, and a\n573:    second projection on them would mix two attachments' state -- with\n574:    a composition error; a reattachment composes a fresh dial with a\n575:    fresh cursor, as `dial` documents. Returns the remote attach!\n576:    result.\"\n577:   [dial descriptor]\n578:   (let [{:keys [channel]} @dial]\n579:     (when-some [attached @channel]\n580:       (throw (ex-info\n581:                \"this dial already attached its one active attachment\"\n582:                {:attachment (:attachment attached)\n583:                 :reattachment \"compose a fresh dial with a fresh cursor\"})))\n584:     (or (establish! dial (:dao.stream/channel descriptor))\n585:         ((:reflect! @channel) descriptor))))\n586: \n587: \n588: (defn dial-resolve!\n589:   \"Resolve the name `n` through the dial's channel, the ws descriptor\n590:    `cd`: dao.stream.remote's link resolve (dao.stream.remote.md 2.4).\n591:    A dial with no channel yet attaches `cd` first, as `dial-attach!`\n592:    does, so a name is resolved before any reflection exists; the\n593:    descriptor a resolve answers is then attached through the same\n594:    channel by `dial-reflect!`. A channel attach that fails answers the\n595:    ws attacher's own outcome. Answers the resolve's outcome: retry\n596:    until the answer is filed, then ok with the remote descriptor and\n597:    surface, or transport-error naming not-found or channel-gone.\"\n598:   [dial cd n]\n599:   (let [{:keys [channel]} @dial]\n600:     (or (when (nil? @channel) (establish! dial cd))\n601:         ((:resolve! @channel) cd n))))\n602: \n603: \n604: (defn dial-reflect!\n605:   \"Attach a further reflection of `descriptor` through a dial's already\n606:    established channel, sharing the one link `dial-attach!` created for\n607:    it: dao.stream.remote.cljc keeps one link per channel descriptor,\n608:    shared by every reflection through that channel, and `attacher`'s\n609:    returned function is exactly that per-channel sharing boundary.  A\n610:    dial with no established channel yet answers `:dao.stream/invalid-\n611:    descriptor`, since there is no attacher to share.\"\n612:   [dial descriptor]\n613:   (let [{:keys [channel]} @dial]\n614:     (if-some [reflect! (:reflect! @channel)]\n615:       (reflect! descriptor)\n616:       {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor})))\n617: \n618: \n619: (defn dial-step!\n620:   \"Drive the dialing composition one tick, at the composition's\n621:    cadence: the attachment's projection first, so what the wire\n622:    deposited reaches the ring, then this end's own mirror step over\n623:    the projected reader and the socket handle, answering the other\n624:    direction's requests against this end's table, each bounded by the\n625:    dial's :step-budget, :mirror-budget and :chase-budget. Given the\n626:    driver's `now`, the link is stepped at it between the two\n627:    (dao.stream.remote.md 2.4, Expiry); when a request is past its\n628:    deadline the channel is lost and the dial, which owns the\n629:    connection, closes the ws handle -- the host then deposits\n630:    :ws/closed and the projection closes the ring. Without `now`\n631:    nothing expires. Returns the mirror's advanced reading cursor.\"\n632:   ([dial]\n633:    (dial-step! dial nil))\n634:   ([dial now]\n635:    (when (some? now)\n636:      (swap! dial assoc :now now))\n637:    (let [{:keys [ring table names channel mirror-cursor step-budget]\n638:           :as d} @dial\n639:          ch @channel]\n640:      (when-some [project (:project ch)]\n641:        (step! project step-budget))\n642:      (let [stepped (when (and (some? now) (:step! ch))\n643:                      ((:step! ch) (:cd ch) now))]\n644:        (when-some [handle (:handle ch)]\n645:          ;; The mirror's effects run once, outside any atom update: the\n646:          ;; driver alone steps the dial, as accept-step! does.\n647:          (reset! mirror-cursor\n648:                  (remote/mirror-step table names ring @mirror-cursor handle\n649:                                      (mirror-bounds d)))\n650:          (when (:dao.stream.remote/channel-gone? stepped)\n651:            (swap! channel assoc :gone? true)\n652:            (when (stream/closable? handle)\n653:              (stream/close! handle)))))\n654:      @mirror-cursor)))\n655: \n656: \n657: (defn channel\n658:   \"The dialed channel as data: {:attachment id :handle h :project p\n659:    :gone? g} -- the ws attachment identity, the ws handle (the channel\n660:    writer), the attachment's projection, and whether a stepped link\n661:    found the channel gone. Nil before the first dial-attach!. A\n662:    composition that owns the connection's lifetime closes the handle\n663:    here.\"\n664:   [dial]\n665:   @(:channel @dial))"}],"deferred":false}}
