{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_f0e27c64846744d3a1f40418","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 300 lines\nNote: showing lines 1-300. More of the file remains. Use offset=301 to continue.\n1: (ns dao.stream.ws-project\n2:   \"The WebSocket channel composition of dao.stream.remote.md (3.1).\n3: \n4:    The mirror and the link of dao.stream.remote speak raw request and\n5:    answer maps, so each channel end composes one step, the projection,\n6:    between the ws deposit medium and the channel: the channel reader is\n7:    a ring buffer the composition wires, the channel writer is the ws\n8:    handle itself. The projection holds the reading cursor on the\n9:    attachment's traffic medium, keeps the events whose :ws/attachment\n10:    names this channel, appends the :ws/value of each :ws/payload onto\n11:    the ring, and drops :ws/error diagnostics. A terminal lifecycle\n12:    event (:ws/closed, :ws/ended) or a failure resolution (:ws/not-found,\n13:    :ws/transport-error) makes the projection close the ring, and so\n14:    does the traffic medium's own end: the projection is over and\n15:    nothing more can arrive, so a link waiting on the ring observes the\n16:    loss instead of blocking forever -- channel loss is then the link's\n17:    own end observation (2.4).\n18: \n19:    The composition helpers wire both ends of the spec's section-5 toy\n20:    over real attachments. The accepting peer drives `accept-step!`:\n21:    endpoint steps, one offer adopted per tick (a fresh traffic medium\n22:    and ring per accepted connection, acknowledged per dao.stream.ws.md\n23:    Serving), then per session the projection and, over the projected\n24:    reader and the socket handle, dao.stream.remote/mirror-step. The\n25:    dialing peer composes `dial` over one ws attacher and drives\n26:    `dial-step!`: the projection and then its own mirror step, so either\n27:    peer serves the other on one connection. Reflections come from\n28:    dao.stream.remote/attacher through the channel end each side holds.\n29:    Every step here is driver-paced: the composition owns the cadence,\n30:    as it does for endpoint-step. Nothing schedules itself.\"\n31:   (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n32:             [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\n33:             [dao.stream.ws :as ws]))\n34: \n35: \n36: (def terminal-events\n37:   \"The deposited events that end the channel: a terminal lifecycle\n38:    event for the attachment (:ws/closed, :ws/ended) or a failure\n39:    resolution (:ws/not-found, :ws/transport-error). The projection\n40:    closes the ring on each of them. :ws/error is a diagnostic and is\n41:    never terminal by itself (dao.stream.ws.md, Deposited events are\n42:    envelopes).\"\n43:   #{:ws/closed :ws/ended :ws/not-found :ws/transport-error})\n44: \n45: \n46: ;; =============================================================================\n47: ;; The projection (3.1's ws-project step)\n48: ;; =============================================================================\n49: \n50: (defn projection\n51:   \"Compose one projection over the attachment named `:attachment` (the\n52:    :ws/attachment value every deposited event of this channel carries),\n53:    the traffic medium reader `:traffic`, the already-minted reading\n54:    cursor `:cursor`, and the ring buffer `:ring` the channel reads.\n55:    The projection owns the cursor from here: each `step!` advances it.\"\n56:   [{:keys [attachment traffic cursor ring]}]\n57:   (when-not (and (some? attachment)\n58:                  (stream/reader? traffic)\n59:                  (some? cursor)\n60:                  (stream/reader? ring)\n61:                  (stream/writer? ring)\n62:                  (stream/closable? ring))\n63:     (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream ws projection composition\"\n64:                     {:attachment attachment :traffic traffic\n65:                      :cursor cursor :ring ring})))\n66:   (atom {:attachment attachment :traffic traffic :cursor cursor\n67:          :ring ring :closed? false}))\n68: \n69: \n70: (defn- project!\n71:   \"Apply one deposited event (3.1): another attachment's event and\n72:    every non-payload, non-terminal kind are ignored here; a :ws/error\n73:    is dropped as a diagnostic; a :ws/payload's :ws/value is appended\n74:    onto the ring; a terminal event or failure resolution closes the\n75:    ring. True only for the terminal case.\"\n76:   [state event]\n77:   (when (= (:ws/attachment event) (:attachment state))\n78:     (let [kind (:ws/event event)]\n79:       (cond\n80:         (= :ws/payload kind)\n81:         (do (when (contains? event :ws/value)\n82:               (stream/append! (:ring state) (:ws/value event)))\n83:             nil)\n84: \n85:         (= :ws/error kind) nil\n86: \n87:         (contains? terminal-events kind)\n88:         (do (stream/close! (:ring state)) true)\n89: \n90:         :else nil))))\n91: \n92: \n93: (defn step!\n94:   \"Drive the projection once, at the composition's cadence: read the\n95:    traffic medium to blocked, keeping, forwarding and dropping per\n96:    3.1, stopping at the event that closes the ring. A gap adopts the\n97:    medium's own recovery cursor, the lost events being lost. The\n98:    medium's own end closes the projection and the ring with it:\n99:    nothing more can arrive, so a link waiting on the ring must\n100:    observe the loss (2.4) rather than block forever. When an optional\n101:    `budget` (positive integer) is provided, read at most `budget`\n102:    events in one step! call; any other non-nil budget is a composition\n103:    error. Returns the projection.\"\n104:   ([project]\n105:    (step! project nil))\n106:   ([project budget]\n107:    (when-not (or (nil? budget) (and (integer? budget) (pos? budget)))\n108:      (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream ws projection step! budget\"\n109:                      {:budget budget})))\n110:    (let [bounded? (some? budget)]\n111:      (loop [remaining (if bounded? budget -1)]\n112:        (if (and bounded? (zero? remaining))\n113:          project\n114:          (let [s @project]\n115:            (if (:closed? s)\n116:              project\n117:              (let [r (stream/next (:traffic s) (:cursor s))]\n118:                (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n119:                  :dao.stream/ok\n120:                  (let [event (:dao.stream/value r)]\n121:                    (swap! project assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n122:                    (if (project! s event)\n123:                      (do (swap! project assoc :closed? true)\n124:                          project)\n125:                      (recur (if bounded? (dec remaining) -1))))\n126: \n127:                  :dao.stream/end\n128:                  (do (stream/close! (:ring s))\n129:                      (swap! project assoc :closed? true)\n130:                      project)\n131: \n132:                  :dao.stream/gap\n133:                  (do (swap! project assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n134:                      (recur (if bounded? (dec remaining) -1)))\n135: \n136:                  ;; blocked, and any read the medium refuses: stay put.\n137:                  project)))))))))\n138: \n139: \n140: (defn closed?\n141:   \"True once the projection stopped: the ring was closed by a terminal\n142:    lifecycle event or a failure resolution, or the traffic medium\n143:    itself answered end.\"\n144:   [project]\n145:   (:closed? @project))\n146: \n147: \n148: (defn reading-cursor\n149:   \"The projection's current reading cursor on the traffic medium.\"\n150:   [project]\n151:   (:cursor @project))\n152: \n153: \n154: ;; =============================================================================\n155: ;; The accepting peer (section 5: accept, project, mirror)\n156: ;; =============================================================================\n157: \n158: (defn- writer-target?\n159:   [x]\n160:   (and (map? x)\n161:        (stream/writer? (:dao.stream/handle x))\n162:        (contains? (:dao.stream/surface x) :writer)))\n163: \n164: \n165: (defn- valid-slot?\n166:   [{:keys [offer-reader offer-cursor ack-writer]}]\n167:   (and (stream/reader? offer-reader)\n168:        (some? offer-cursor)\n169:        (writer-target? ack-writer)))\n170: \n171: \n172: (defn- pos-int-or-nil?\n173:   [x]\n174:   (or (nil? x) (and (integer? x) (pos? x))))\n175: \n176: \n177: (defn- mirror-bounds\n178:   \"The remote/mirror-step bounds of an acceptor or dial state.\"\n179:   [{:keys [mirror-budget chase-budget]}]\n180:   {:dao.stream.remote/mirror-budget mirror-budget\n181:    :dao.stream.remote/chase-budget chase-budget})\n182: \n183: \n184: (defn make-acceptor\n185:   \"Compose the accepting end of the spec's section-5 toy.\n186:    `:endpoint` is a dao.stream.ws/make-endpoint value whose handoff\n187:    `:slots` are given here, in endpoint order, as {:offer-reader r\n188:    :offer-cursor c :ack-writer target} -- readers, cursors and writers\n189:    the composition minted before the listener started. `:table` is the\n190:    mirror's table (dao.stream.remote.md 2.2). `:make-media` receives\n191:    one accepted offer and returns the attachment's composition:\n192:    :traffic (the deposit target the acknowledgement carries),\n193:    :admission (its declaration), :reader (the traffic reader the\n194:    projection reads), :cursor (its minted reading cursor) and :ring\n195:    (the fresh channel ring buffer). `:names`, optional, is the name\n196:    map beside the table (dao.stream.remote.md section 2), {name\n197:    identity}, each value a key of the table: the mirror answers a\n198:    named descriptor request from it. `:max-sessions`, optional positive\n199:    integer or nil, bounds concurrent active sessions. `:idle-timeout`,\n200:    optional positive integer milliseconds or nil, sets idle session\n201:    expiry against the `now` given to accept-step!; its alias\n202:    `:idle-timeout-ms` takes precedence when both are given.\n203:    `:step-budget`, optional positive integer or nil, bounds the events\n204:    each session's projection reads per tick. `:mirror-budget` and\n205:    `:chase-budget`, optional positive integers or nil, bound each\n206:    session's mirror per tick (dao.stream.remote/mirror-step bounds).\n207:    The listener is the\n208:    host's: it calls ws/accept-connection! on this endpoint, per\n209:    dao.stream.ws.md Serving.\"\n210:   [{:keys [endpoint slots table names make-media max-sessions\n211:            idle-timeout-ms idle-timeout step-budget mirror-budget\n212:            chase-budget] :as config}]\n213:   (let [idle-t (or idle-timeout-ms idle-timeout)]\n214:     (when-not (and (map? config)\n215:                    (some? endpoint)\n216:                    (fn? make-media)\n217:                    (map? table)\n218:                    (or (nil? names) (map? names))\n219:                    (or (nil? max-sessions)\n220:                        (and (integer? max-sessions) (pos? max-sessions)))\n221:                    (or (nil? idle-t)\n222:                        (and (integer? idle-t) (pos? idle-t)))\n223:                    (or (nil? step-budget)\n224:                        (and (integer? step-budget) (pos? step-budget)))\n225:                    (or (nil? mirror-budget)\n226:                        (and (integer? mirror-budget) (pos? mirror-budget)))\n227:                    (or (nil? chase-budget)\n228:                        (and (integer? chase-budget) (pos? chase-budget)))\n229:                    (seq slots)\n230:                    (every? valid-slot? slots))\n231:       (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream ws acceptor composition\"\n232:                       {:config config})))\n233:     (atom {:endpoint endpoint\n234:            :slots (vec slots)\n235:            :table table\n236:            :names names\n237:            :make-media make-media\n238:            :max-sessions max-sessions\n239:            :idle-timeout idle-t\n240:            :step-budget step-budget\n241:            :mirror-budget mirror-budget\n242:            :chase-budget chase-budget\n243:            :offer-cursors (mapv :offer-cursor slots)\n244:            :sessions {}})))\n245: \n246: \n247: (defn- session-closed?\n248:   \"True if the session's projection is closed, or the session was explicitly\n249:    marked closed.\"\n250:   [s]\n251:   (or (:closed? s)\n252:       (closed? (:project s))))\n253: \n254: \n255: (defn- session-idle?\n256:   \"True if the session has exceeded idle-timeout given `now`.\"\n257:   [s idle-timeout now]\n258:   (and (some? idle-timeout)\n259:        (some? now)\n260:        (number? (:last-activity-ms s))\n261:        (>= (- now (:last-activity-ms s)) idle-timeout)))\n262: \n263: \n264: (defn- close-session-resources!\n265:   \"Close a session's socket handle and channel ring.\"\n266:   [s]\n267:   (when (stream/closable? (:handle s))\n268:     (stream/close! (:handle s)))\n269:   (when (stream/closable? (:ring s))\n270:     (stream/close! (:ring s))))\n271: \n272: \n273: (defn- reaped\n274:   \"The sessions without closed or expired ones. A closed session's tick\n275:    just ran its last mirror pass -- a closed ring forwards no further\n276:    request, so only what it retained could ever be answered, and that\n277:    pass answered what the handle accepted -- so its handle, ring and\n278:    projection have nothing left to do. Keeping them would grow the\n279:    composition without bound across repeated connections; the endpoint\n280:    released the connection's slot at acceptance (dao.stream.ws.md\n281:    Serving), and this is the composition's own bound. When idle-timeout\n282:    and `now` are supplied, a session idle for at least idle-timeout is\n283:    reaped too, its handle and ring closed: unlike a closed session's,\n284:    its connection may still be open.\"\n285:   [m idle-timeout now]\n286:   (reduce-kv\n287:     (fn [acc att s]\n288:       (cond\n289:         (session-closed? s) acc\n290: \n291:         (session-idle? s idle-timeout now)\n292:         (do (close-session-resources! s) acc)\n293: \n294:         :else (assoc acc att s)))\n295:     {}\n296:     m))\n297: \n298: \n299: (defn- reap-sessions!\n300:   \"Reap closed or expired sessions from the acceptor atom and return"}],"deferred":false}}
