{"type":"event","event":{"type":"thinking_end","text":"Note: `links` validates drain-budget, max-outstanding, max-filed, give-up-after — but does NOT validate `:dao.stream.remote/budget` (prefetch stamp). The production-bounds `link-policy` check in serve covers what links validates. In serve, `(link-policy b)` calls `(remote/links policy)` with only the policy keys — but doesn't include `:dao.stream.remote/channels`, so `channels` becomes nil... `(contains? nil cd)` — contains? against nil throws an exception in Clojure (\"contains? not supported on type: clojure.lang.PersistentArrayMap\"? No — contains? on nil throws NullPointerException? Actually `(contains? nil 1)` → error \"contains? not supported on type: nil\"?). But that's only inside the attach function, not at construction time. At construction, `(def by-channel (atom {}))` and the closure are fine. So the `(remote/links policy)` call succeeds and validates the four bounds. OK.\n\nAlso note: `:dao.stream.remote/budget` is NOT validated by links — the spec's table says the \"link (prefetch stamp)\" layer enforces it. Let me check new-link to see whether budget gets validated. Line 349 has `:events (:dao.stream.remote/events policy)`. I'll check budget validation around lines 336-360."}}
