{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_fec0ade3185f4dc896e56c1e","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 30 lines\nNote: showing lines 770-799. More of the file remains. Use offset=800 to continue.\n770:   handle to bound a peer that never completes the handshake. `yin.repl`\n771:   is this gap's first consumer and `dao.jing.remote` (deprecated by\n772:   `dao.stream.remote.md`) its second, and neither can close it from where\n773:   it stands.\n774: - Exact envelope key set (tracks the contract's descriptor TBD).\n775: - Liveness: for a connection used as a `dao.stream.remote.md` channel,\n776:   request liveness is decided there (2.4, Expiry): a request unanswered\n777:   past `:dao.stream.remote/give-up-after`, against the `now` a driver hands\n778:   the link's step, loses the channel, and the dial closes this handle.\n779:   The idle probe is the consumer's own periodic read and its deadline: a\n780:   reader that polls sends a `next` the mirror answers, and an unanswered\n781:   one expires; its cadence is the composition's. No protocol ping/pong is\n782:   composed, and the open question is closed for channels used through\n783:   `dao.stream.remote` (`dao.stream.remote-channel`). Probing an idle\n784:   connection used outside a remote channel remains open.\n785: - Resumption protocol: stream identity is stable across reconnects, so\n786:   resumption is possible by design; what history a rejoining dialer receives\n787:   (and how it states where it left off) is not yet specified for the copy\n788:   path. Through `dao.stream.remote.md` a kept cursor is the whole answer.\n789: - Backpressure protocols above the stream (a reader publishing its progress\n790:   as data is interpretation, outside both this transport and the contract).\n791:   Needing nothing from this transport does not mean needing no specification:\n792:   a pause vocabulary both ends must recognize is interoperable wire content,\n793:   and it requires a durable home before it is built. `dao.lease.md` is the\n794:   intended home for its semantics and does not yet claim them; the wire form\n795:   is owed by neither that document nor this one until it does. The v2\n796:   migration plan has deferred flow control out of its slice for the same\n797:   reason, so nothing is being built against an unsettled vocabulary.\n798: - Two host seams (http-kit server, Dart) expose no outbound backlog after\n799:   establishment. There `:ws/outbound-high-water` does not apply, `append!`"}],"deferred":false}}
