{"type":"event","event":{"type":"thinking_end","text":"Documentation fixes are reflected. Now, some remaining verification items:\n\n1. Check the restart case in head_ws_test.cljc and the real-socket JVM case — confirm that moving the fixtures hasn't changed semantics. In particular, `unlisten!` deposits `:stopped`, and the behavior of head.ws's `observe` on `:stopped`: lines 256-257 `(assoc server :status :stopped)` — so head.ws's server becomes :stopped. In the restart test, the old server is simply replaced. And head.ws's serve-step at :stopped — need to confirm it doesn't break. According to the engineer, tests pass. Can't run tests in plan mode (shell is blocked). This is a review-level constraint worth noting — actually, running tests is nearly read-only but is blocked. Note it.\n\nWait — actually there's one potential regression from deviation #8: in head_ws_test, is there any case that calls `unlisten!` and then continues to step the old server expecting :serving? Example: dht restart flow. The engineer states only the restart case uses it. head.ws's observe maps :stopped → :status :stopped, and serve-step presumably returns stopped servers as-is. The test then creates a new server afterward. Claimed to pass.\n\n2. Confirm the use of `closed!` in loopback-net: `close-conn!` calls the server-side closed! and then the client-side closed!. The original head_ws fixture may have been in the same order. No problem.\n\n3. Check remote_channel_test's `stop-while-starting-and-stop-twice`: quiet's bind doesn't deposit bind-succeeded and returns an ok map with :port. Server is :starting. stop! → :stopping. First serve-step 0: begin-stop → accept-step!, release!, since=0, unbind! → net/unbind-on... wait, the host has :unbind! (counting? no — the host is host-of with only bind! changed). unbind-on deposits :stopped on pump and dissocs the listener by (:port listener) — listener is {:dao.stream/outcome :ok :port (:bind-port opts)} → dissocs port 9. OK. Then serve-step 1: continue-stop → drain-lifecycle finds :stopped → confirmed. ✓ Test pumps before serve-step 1. ✓\n\n4. Another potential defect: `begin-stop` sets `:stop :since now` before unbind!. If unbind fails → stopped with ::unbind-failed but :since is set. No problem.\n\n5. `continue-stop` grace check: `(>= (- now since) stop-grace-ms)`. Test: since=1000, grace=100; serve-step 1099 → 99 < 100 → still stopping; at 1100 → 100 ≥ 100 → stopped. ✓ Note: continue-stop at 1099 also does accept-step! and endpoint-stop! — harmless.\n\n6. Edge: `drain-lifecycle` inside continue-stop can transition to :stopped :confirmed before the grace check — guarded by `(= :stopping (:status server))`. ✓\n\n7. `observe`'s catch-all `(= :stopped kind)` — what about a :stopped fact arriving during :refused or :stopped state? drain-lifecycle only runs while status is live (contains? live). Once refused/stopped, no further draining. ✓ But note: the drain-lifecycle loop checks `(contains? live (:status server))` before reading the next fact — once status becomes :stopped mid-drain, the remaining facts stay in the medium. No problem.\n\n8. `sessions` — `(some-> (:acceptor server) ws-project/sessions)`. For refused server (select-keys only [:spec :descriptor]) → nil. ✓\n\n9. Missing :lifecycle/:lifecycle-cursor keys on refused-from-bind-failed server (select-keys drops them). If serve-step is called on the refused server, it returns as-is (default of case). ✓\n\n10. `descriptor-of` with nil path → identity \"ws://h:p\" + nil → does (str nil) become \"\"? (str \"ws://\" \"h\" \":\" 9 nil) → \"ws://h:9\". ws/descriptor? may require path to be a string. Does serve validate path? No, there's no path validation — a spec without :path produces a descriptor with :ws/path nil. Does make-endpoint validate the descriptor? Need to check the requirements of descriptor? — canonical-path? Let me check ws/descriptor?.\n\nLet me read lines 50-130 of ws.cljc to see descriptor?/canonical-path?/checked-bounds and make-endpoint."}}
{"type":"event","event":{"type":"text_delta","delta":"Let"}}
