{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_1279e1d423ff4d578754d30e","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 90 lines\nNote: showing lines 50-139. More of the file remains. Use offset=140 to continue.\n50: (defn- outcome\n51:   [x]\n52:   {:dao.stream/outcome x})\n53: \n54: \n55: (defn canonical-path?\n56:   \"True for the already-canonical request-target form carried on a descriptor.\n57:    URI parsing and bind policy belong to the host adapter; this gate prevents a\n58:    query, fragment, relative path, or unresolved dot segment from reaching the\n59:    exact served-path lookup.\"\n60:   [path]\n61:   (and (string? path)\n62:        (not (empty? path))\n63:        (str/starts-with? path \"/\")\n64:        (not (str/includes? path \"?\"))\n65:        (not (str/includes? path \"#\"))\n66:        (not (some #{\".\" \"..\"} (str/split path #\"/\")))))\n67: \n68: \n69: (defn descriptor?\n70:   \"The settled WebSocket descriptor gate.  It names a served stream, not a\n71:    particular connection, and contains only portable reachability data.\n72:    The one-argument form keeps the Transit domain as the public default; a\n73:    composition selecting a codec profile gates the same descriptor against\n74:    that profile's domain.\"\n75:   ([x] (descriptor? x transit/profile))\n76:   ([x codec]\n77:    (and (map? x)\n78:         (= transport-type (:dao.stream/type x))\n79:         (string? (:dao.stream/identity x))\n80:         (string? (:ws/host x))\n81:         (integer? (:ws/port x))\n82:         (pos? (:ws/port x))\n83:         (canonical-path? (:ws/path x))\n84:         ((:ws/portable-value? codec) x))))\n85: \n86: \n87: (defn admission?\n88:   \"Assembly-time declaration required for every transport deposit medium.\"\n89:   [x]\n90:   (and (map? x)\n91:        (= :evict-oldest (:retention x))\n92:        (integer? (:capacity x))\n93:        (pos? (:capacity x))\n94:        (contains? #{:host-values :portable-values} (:value-domain x))))\n95: \n96: \n97: (defn- writer-target?\n98:   [x]\n99:   (and (map? x)\n100:        (stream/writer? (:dao.stream/handle x))\n101:        (contains? (:dao.stream/surface x) :writer)))\n102: \n103: \n104: (defn- checked-target\n105:   [target declaration]\n106:   (when-not (and (writer-target? target) (admission? declaration))\n107:     (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream WebSocket deposit composition\"\n108:                     {:target target :admission declaration})))\n109:   target)\n110: \n111: \n112: (defn- attachment-id\n113:   []\n114:   (str (random-uuid)))\n115: \n116: \n117: (def ^:private bound-keys\n118:   \"The byte and frame bounds a composition may set on `make-attacher` and\n119:    `make-endpoint`.  Each is a positive integer or nil; nil is unbounded.\"\n120:   [:ws/max-frame-bytes :ws/max-pending-frames :ws/max-pending-bytes\n121:    :ws/outbound-high-water :ws/max-outbound-bytes])\n122: \n123: \n124: (defn- checked-bounds\n125:   [config]\n126:   (let [bounds (select-keys config bound-keys)]\n127:     (when-not (every? (fn [[_ v]] (or (nil? v) (and (integer? v) (pos? v)))) bounds)\n128:       (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream WebSocket bounds\" {:bounds bounds})))\n129:     bounds))\n130: \n131: \n132: (defn- payload-size\n133:   \"The raw size of one wire payload: characters for a text payload, bytes\n134:    for host bytes.  `:cljd` comes first because the cljd host-eval pass also\n135:    reads a `:clj` branch.\"\n136:   [payload]\n137:   (if (string? payload)\n138:     (count payload)\n139:     #?(:cljd (.-length ^List payload)"}],"deferred":false}}
