{"type":"event","event":{"type":"message_update","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"(Thinking) In this environment, writes are completely blocked (even writes to the plans directory require permissions). Therefore, the report cannot be written. The review results should be presented inline within the response, with a note attached stating that the write failed.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I can't write files in this environment (even the plan file is blocked), so here's the completed review inline — it's ready to be saved as `collab/1791388000000-reviewer-stream-s3a-1.qwen3.8-max.findings.md`.\n\n# Reviewer: adversarial review of Track B Slice S3a-1\n\nReviewed the full working tree against the architect spec and engineer report: `ws.cljc` (`endpoint-stop!`), `ws_project.cljc` (`stop!`, `close-sessions!`, `adopt!` stopping branch, `dial-step!` `:gone?`), `remote_channel.cljc` (whole), all four test files, the moved `loopback_net.cljc` fixture, and both design-doc amendments. Method note: read-only pass — `git diff` and test runs were unavailable here, so the engineer's green-run claims are taken on report and re-verified at landing.\n\n## Verdict: ACCEPT\n\n## 1. Spec conformance (blocking points, all pass)\n\n- **§4.1 `endpoint-stop!`** (ws.cljc:762–780): phase `:closed` → 1001 `dao.stream/endpoint-stopped` → `terminal!` `:ws/closed` → `release-slot!`, per pending slot; idempotent; `terminal!`'s `:terminal?` guard keeps the terminal event exactly-once even against a synchronous host close callback.\n- **§4.2**: `stop!` is a pure `swap!`; `adopt!`'s `(not (:stopping? @acceptor))` guard (line 331) rejects exactly like the cap. Slot release never depends on the close callback — the second `endpoint-step` in `accept-step!` releases on the `:closed` phase. `close-sessions!` runs outside `swap!`, driver-only, like `reap-sessions!`.\n- **§4.3**: `begin-stop` = last bounded answering pass → `release!` (stop! + close-sessions! + endpoint-stop!) → `unbind!`, with `::unbind-failed` stopping at once; `continue-stop` completes on `:stopped` fact / lifecycle gap / `stop-grace-ms` against driver `now`. No clock, no sleep. `stop!` does no I/O (test asserts unbind count 0).\n- **§1 profile**: all 20 rows with exact values; validation delegated to `make-endpoint`, `make-acceptor`, `remote/links`, all before `bind!` (test asserts nothing listened on invalid bounds).\n- **§2.1**: full API surface present; `bind!`/`unbind!` called with exactly the documented `yin.repl.host` seam shapes, so S3b plugs in cleanly; refusals are data.\n- **§5.1/§5.2**: every lifecycle-table cell implemented; the evicted-close-event row works via `:gone?` and is directly tested. Nothing touches `:installed`, no invented gaps.\n- **§7**: all 15 remote-channel cases landed with spec'd names, plus the `ws_test` and two `ws_project_test` cases.\n- **Invariants**: no ambient scheduler (every deadline is driver `now`), no new core stream op (`dao/stream.cljc` untouched), transport neutrality held (yin sources untouched; spec carries no `:ws/` key, asserted).\n\n## 2. Deviations 1–9: all accepted\n\n1. **20 keys, not 17** — correct; the §1 table has 20 rows.\n2. **Structural `::invalid-table`** — *more* right than the spec: `make-acceptor` only checks `(map? table)` and never throws on entry cursors, so the spec's definition was unimplementable as written.\n3. **Pending-at-stop closed by `adopt!` (1000), not 1001** — a direct consequence of the spec's own §4.3 order; 1000 \"detached\" is the reattachable close the ws design assigns. 1001 path covered in `ws_test` and the lifecycle-lost case.\n4. **Later stopping ticks run `accept-step!` + `endpoint-stop!`** — necessary: without it closed sessions never reap and racing pendings leak.\n5. **host-stopped also calls `ws-project/stop!`; `:stopped` while starting = host-stopped** — closes real holes.\n6. **Newcomer-during-stop outcome** — observable dial status matches spec intent.\n7. **Double poll (`ask!`)** — required; a single poll is answered from the prefetched local `blocked` and never reaches the wire.\n8. **`unlisten!` deposits `:stopped`** — `head.ws` observe already handled `:stopped`; restart case unaffected.\n9. **`head.ws` untouched** — matches the §8 landing table.\n\nThe undocumented `:gone?` addition is a genuine gap-filler (evicted `:ws/closed` + expired link would otherwise leave the dial `:attached` forever), additive for existing consumers, and directly tested.\n\n## 3. Findings (non-blocking)\n\n- **F1 (minor, edge)**: a host *without* `:unbind!` stops as `::unbind-failed` with a live listener — after `:stopped`, `serve-step` is inert, so later-accepted connections sit `:pending` forever (endpoint expiry never runs again). Real assemblies always provide `:unbind!`; fix in S3b (treat absent `:unbind!` as the grace path, or keep `endpoint-stop!` running while pendings exist).\n- **F2 (nit)**: `endpoint-stop!` ignores `invoke-close!` failure — no `:ws/error :ws/close-failure` diagnostic as `close!`/`close-ended!` emit. Bookkeeping unaffected.\n- **F3 (nit)**: `::host-stopped` yields `:stop {:outcome …}` without `:since` (assoc onto nil).\n- **F4 (robustness)**: an explicit `{:stop-grace-ms nil}` override would throw in `continue-stop`'s `>=`; unvalidated key.\n- **F5 (spec text)**: §"}]}}
