ayload)))\n207:         result))))\n208: \n209: "}]},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_61a578eed939479aa1e820d5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 160 lines\nNote: showing lines 300-459. More of the file remains. Use offset=460 to continue.\n300:   \"Reap closed or expired sessions from the acceptor atom and return\n301:    the kept sessions. Reaping closes handles, so it runs outside swap!;\n302:    the driver alone steps the acceptor.\"\n303:   [acceptor now]\n304:   (let [{:keys [sessions idle-timeout]} @acceptor\n305:         kept (reaped sessions idle-timeout now)]\n306:     (swap! acceptor assoc :sessions kept)\n307:     kept))\n308: \n309: \n310: (defn- adopt!\n311:   \"Adopt one accepted offer as a session: create the attachment's\n312:    media through :make-media, acknowledge the offer per\n313:    dao.stream.ws.md Serving (:ws/command :ws/accept, the deposit\n314:    target and its admission), and register the projection, ring,\n315:    reading cursor and socket handle the mirror works through. An\n316:    offer that is not an acceptance, and an acknowledgement the slot's\n317:    medium refuses, close the offered handle; the slot itself is the\n318:    endpoint's to release. When :max-sessions is reached after reaping\n319:    expired/closed sessions, reject the newcomer by closing its handle\n320:    without an accept acknowledgement. A :make-media or acknowledgement\n321:    append that throws is isolated the same way: the offered handle is\n322:    closed, no session is registered, and the tick goes on. A :make-media\n323:    that throws after allocating a ring leaks that ring; avoiding it is\n324:    the composition's own concern, the acceptor retains nothing. A\n325:    stopping acceptor (`stop!`) rejects every offer the way the cap\n326:    does: the handle closed, no acknowledgement, no media.\"\n327:   [acceptor slot offer now]\n328:   (let [handle (get-in offer [:ws/handle :dao.stream/handle])\n329:         attachment (:ws/attachment offer)]\n330:     (if-not (and (= :ws/accepted (:ws/event offer))\n331:                  (not (:stopping? @acceptor))\n332:                  (string? attachment)\n333:                  (some? handle)\n334:                  (stream/writer? handle)\n335:                  (stream/closable? handle))\n336:       (when (stream/closable? handle)\n337:         (stream/close! handle))\n338:       (let [cur-sessions (reap-sessions! acceptor now)\n339:             max-s (:max-sessions @acceptor)]\n340:         (if (and (some? max-s) (>= (count cur-sessions) max-s))\n341:           ;; Reject newcomer at active cap\n342:           (when (stream/closable? handle)\n343:             (stream/close! handle))\n344:           (let [make-media (:make-media @acceptor)\n345:                 [media appended]\n346:                 (try\n347:                   (let [media (make-media offer)]\n348:                     [media (stream/append!\n349:                              (:dao.stream/handle (:ack-writer slot))\n350:                              {:ws/attachment attachment\n351:                               :ws/command :ws/accept\n352:                               :ws/deposit (:traffic media)\n353:                               :ws/admission (:admission media)})])\n354:                   (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n355:                     nil))]\n356:             (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome appended))\n357:               (swap! acceptor assoc-in [:sessions attachment]\n358:                      {:attachment attachment\n359:                       :handle handle\n360:                       :ring (:ring media)\n361:                       :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n362:                                 (stream/cursor (:ring media)\n363:                                                stream/anchor-oldest))\n364:                       :project (projection\n365:                                  {:attachment attachment\n366:                                   :traffic (:reader media)\n367:                                   :cursor (:cursor media)\n368:                                   :ring (:ring media)})\n369:                       :last-activity-ms (or now 0)})\n370:               (stream/close! handle))))))))\n371: \n372: \n373: (defn accept-step!\n374:   \"Advance the accepting composition one tick at `now`, in the order\n375:    serving compositions use: a transport step first (releasing dead\n376:    pendings, consuming standing acknowledgements), then one offer per\n377:    slot adopted with its fresh media and acknowledgement, then a second\n378:    transport step, so the fresh acknowledgement is consumed and the\n379:    accept frame is on the wire before this end answers anything,\n380:    then per session the projection and, over the projected reader and\n381:    the socket handle, the mirror step. Each session step is isolated in\n382:    a try/catch so an unexpected error marks the session closed and frees\n383:    its resources without bringing down the acceptor loop or healthy\n384:    peers. A session whose projection has closed or which has timed out\n385:    is then removed: repeated connections must not accumulate. Returns\n386:    the acceptor.\"\n387:   [acceptor now]\n388:   (let [{:keys [endpoint slots] :as s} @acceptor]\n389:     (ws/endpoint-step endpoint now)\n390:     (doseq [[index slot] (map-indexed vector slots)]\n391:       (let [r (stream/next (:offer-reader slot)\n392:                            (nth (:offer-cursors s) index))]\n393:         (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n394:           (swap! acceptor assoc-in [:offer-cursors index]\n395:                  (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n396:           (adopt! acceptor slot (:dao.stream/value r) now))))\n397:     (ws/endpoint-step endpoint now)\n398:     (doseq [[attachment session] (:sessions @acceptor)]\n399:       (try\n400:         (let [read-from (reading-cursor (:project session))\n401:               _ (step! (:project session) (:step-budget @acceptor))\n402:               cursor (remote/mirror-step (:table @acceptor)\n403:                                          (:names @acceptor)\n404:                                          (:ring session)\n405:                                          (:cursor session)\n406:                                          (:handle session)\n407:                                          (mirror-bounds @acceptor))\n408:               active? (or (not= read-from (reading-cursor (:project session)))\n409:                           (not= (:cursor session) cursor))]\n410:           (swap! acceptor update-in [:sessions attachment]\n411:                  #(cond-> (assoc % :cursor cursor)\n412:                     (and active? (some? now)) (assoc :last-activity-ms now))))\n413:         (catch #?(:clj Throwable :cljs :default :cljd Object) _\n414:           ;; Isolate the failure: close this session, spare the rest.\n415:           (close-session-resources! session)\n416:           (swap! acceptor assoc-in [:sessions attachment :closed?] true))))\n417:     (reap-sessions! acceptor now)\n418:     acceptor))\n419: \n420: \n421: (defn sessions\n422:   \"The acceptor's sessions as data: attachment id -> {:attachment\n423:    :handle :ring :cursor :project :last-activity-ms}.\"\n424:   [acceptor]\n425:   (:sessions @acceptor))\n426: \n427: \n428: (defn stop!\n429:   \"Mark the acceptor stopping (dao.stream.remote.md 3.0, Explicit\n430:    stop). From here every offer is rejected as at the session cap; the\n431:    sessions already adopted are still projected and mirrored by\n432:    accept-step!, so one more tick is the last bounded answering pass.\n433:    Performs no I/O. Returns the acceptor.\"\n434:   [acceptor]\n435:   (swap! acceptor assoc :stopping? true)\n436:   acceptor)\n437: \n438: \n439: (defn close-sessions!\n440:   \"Close every session's socket handle and channel ring and mark it\n441:    closed; the next accept-step! reaps the