en -- ok with the remote descriptor of\n1138:    the stream the name maps to, its own identity over that channel,\n1139:    and the entry's declared surface under :dao.stream.remote/surface;\n1140:    the not-found error as transport-error with reason not-found;\n1141:    otherwise the named descriptor request is sent when none is\n1142:    outstanding and the answer is transport-error with\n1143:    :dao.stream/retry? true, as cursor answers. After channel loss the\n1144:    answer is transport-error naming channel-gone. A channel this peer\n1145:    does not reach is not-found. `(h channel-descriptor now)` is the\n1146:    driver's step of that channel's link at `now` (link-step!): nil for\n1147:    a channel this peer does not reach, otherwise\n1148:    {:dao.stream.remote/channel-gone? bool :dao.stream.remote/expired\n1149:    id-or-nil}. Without a stepped `now` nothing expires. `opts` is\n1150:    `attacher`'s; a bound among them (:dao.stream.remote/drain-budget,\n1151:    max-outstanding, max-filed, give-up-after) that is neither nil nor a\n1152:    positive integer is a composition error.\"\n1153:   [opts]\n1154:   (let [channels (:dao.stream.remote/channels opts)\n1155:         policy (select-keys opts [:dao.stream.remote/events\n1156:                                   :dao.stream.remote/resend-after\n1157:                                   :dao.stream.remote/budget\n1158:                                   :dao.stream.remote/drain-budget\n1159:                                   :dao.stream.remote/max-outstanding\n1160:                                   :dao.stream.remote/max-filed\n1161:                                   :dao.stream.remote/give-up-after])\n1162:         _ (when-not (every? #(pos-int-or-nil? (get policy %))\n1163:                             [:dao.stream.remote/drain-budget\n1164:                              :dao.stream.remote/max-outstanding\n1165:                              :dao.stream.remote/max-filed\n1166:                              :dao.stream.remote/give-up-after])\n1167:             (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream remote link policy\"\n1168:                             {:policy policy})))\n1169:         by-channel (atom {})\n1170:         link-for! (fn [cd]\n1171:                     (swap! by-channel\n1172:                            (fn [m]\n1173:                              (if (contains? m cd)\n1174:                                m\n1175:                                (assoc m cd\n1176:                                       (new-link cd (get channels cd)\n1177:                                                 policy)))))\n1178:                     (get @by-channel cd))]\n1179:     {:attach\n1180:      (fn [descriptor]\n1181:        (if-not (valid-remote-descriptor? descriptor)\n1182:          (result :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor)\n1183:          (let [cd (:dao.stream/channel descriptor)]\n1184:            (if-not (contains? channels cd)\n1185:              (result :dao.stream/not-found)\n1186:              (let [link (link-for! cd)\n1187:                    refl (atom {:link link\n1188:                                :descriptor descriptor\n1189:                                :identity (:dao.stream/identity descriptor)\n1190:                                :surface nil\n1191:                                :source-descriptor nil\n1192:                                :gone? false\n1193:                                :closed? false\n1194:                                :ids #{}})]"}]}],"meta":{"source":"tool","messageId":"dbfbaf8b-551a-42f9-b097-d13ffd34f57d"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Note: `links` validates drain-budget, max-outstanding, max-filed, give-up-after — but does NOT validate `:dao.stream.remote/budget` (prefetch stamp). The production-bounds `link-policy` check in serve covers what links validates. In serve, `(link-policy b)` calls `(remote/links policy)` with only the policy keys — but doesn't include `:dao.stream.remote/channels`, so `channels` becomes nil... `(contains? nil cd)` — contains? against nil throws an exception in Clojure (\"contains? not supported on type: clojure.lang.PersistentArrayMap\"? No — contains? on nil throws NullPointerException? Actually `(contains? nil 1)` → error \"contains? not supported on type: nil\"?). But that's only inside the attach function, not at construction time. At construction, `(def by-channel (atom {}))` and the closure are fine. So the `(remote/links policy)` call succeeds and validates the four bounds. OK.\n\nAlso note: `:dao.stream.remote/budget` is NOT validated by links — the spec's table says the \"link (prefetch stamp)\" layer enforces it. Let me check new-link to see whether budget gets validated. Line 349 has `:events (:dao.stream.remote/events policy)`. I'll check budget validation around lines 336-360.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_35302cfc8eea4495baa38cd0","name":"read_file","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc","offset":330,"limit":60}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1791393200515,"messageId":"4fe976d0-3af9-487d-8ca5-64eef6de734a"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_35302cfc8eea4495baa38cd0","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 60 lines\nNote: showing lines 330-389. More of the file remains. Use offset=390 to continue.\n330:    writer has refused, kept unsent with the reflection each was sent\n331:    for; filed answers keyed by id; the more outcomes installed at\n332:    their served identity and the cursor that precedes each; an\n333:    optional event writer; and the policy data -- the resend-after k,\n334:    the budget k stamped on next requests, and the bounds on reads per\n335:    drain, on outstanding plus kept requests and on filed plus\n336:    installed answers, and the give-up-after liveness bound, all\n337:    composition data; and the last `now` a driver stepped it at.\"\n338:   [cd chan poli