rce":"tool","messageId":"cdc1ab1f-2edf-4f7c-8385-ff06c834b832"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"emit! uses stream/append! against the writer — the test is passing the raw ring handle. append! works on handles. OK.\n\nNext, check the diff of head_ws_test.cljc — this test was changed to use the moved fixture. Also check docs. Also compare `loopback-literal?` with the old head.ws's `loopback?`. Furthermore, verify that `descriptor?` accepts this descriptor, and also check the value of `ws/transport-type`.\n\nAlso, should I verify the engineer's claim about the test count? I can't run tests (shell is blocked). I'll note that in the review.\n\nLet me check loopback? in head/ws.cljc and where the fixture is used in head_ws_test.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_3602e4356c5e422bb65fb61e","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"loopback|ipv6|octet","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc","output_mode":"content","-n":true,"-C":4}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_a9a6e57e82f24205960de4a1","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"loopback-net|loopback_net|net/","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/test/yin/vm/linker/head_ws_test.cljc","output_mode":"content","-n":true,"head_limit":30}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1791393211424,"messageId":"76efcd6f-d50b-4a0a-a0c4-6a59fe147d59"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_3602e4356c5e422bb65fb61e","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-1-(ns yin.vm.linker.head.ws\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc:2:  \"The head board over WebSocket, on loopback\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-3-   (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md 5.1, section 6, slice H2).\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-4-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-5-   The only namespace of the head trace that knows a transport.  Both\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-6-   ends are thin compositions of `dao.stream.ws-project`:\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-9-     the board under the ring's own identity with surface #{:reader},\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-10-     and a one-entry name map, the board name to that identity.  It\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-11-     listens at path /head.  The listener is an argument, the host's\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-12-     `listen!` of the `yin.repl.host` seam shape.  A bind host that is\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc:13:     not a loopback literal composes no endpoint.  `serve-step` drives\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-14-     it at the composition's cadence.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-15-   * `dial` composes the reader's end over the host's `connect!`, the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-16-     ws attacher's host seam: it resolves the board name, then attaches\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-17-     the descriptor answered.  `dial-step` drives it; `handle` is the\n--\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-64-;; =============================================================================\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-65-;; Loopback literals\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-66-;; =============================================================================\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s3a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc-67-\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head/ws.cljc:68:(def ^:private ipv6-loopb